 table('residuals.csv',rows);dump('comparison.json',{'schema':'conditional-model-data-comparison-106','models':summaries,'statisticalDefinition':'sigma_stat=(sigma_minus+sigma_plus)/2; Q=sum((vobs-vmodel)^2/sigma^2). Asymmetric original errors remain in plots and data.','systematicDefinition':'Sensitivity scenario sigma_i^2=sigma_stat^2+(fraction_Jiao*vobs)^2; not a measured full covariance. Additional correlated scenario C=D+outer(0.02*vobs,0.02*vobs), explicitly assumed coherent scale mode motivated by Jiao section2.1. Neither is asserted as unique covariance.','interpretation':'Conditional residual diagnostics, not calibrated chi-square hypothesis tests, Bayes factors, sigma detections or formal evidence of a unique halo. No parameter fitted here; historical observational calibration and missing gas/CGM prevent claiming38 independent out-of-sample degrees of freedom.','baryonicSensitivity':'Both models retain identical fixed baryons; neither halo nor baryons fitted freely. A baryon-only refit, gas or other density family would be a separate model and is not silently introduced.','fittedParameters':[],'observationalCovarianceAvailable':False})
